From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon McGinty <brandon.mcginty@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:19:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] speakup: reject malformed UTF-8 in synth_utf8_get

`synth_utf8_get` accepted any sequence whose continuation bytes carried
the 0x80 bit pattern, so `synth_utf8_get` accepted three classes of
sequence that encode no Unicode scalar value.

An overlong form encodes a value that a shorter sequence already
encodes, for example 0xc0 0x80 for U+0000.  A surrogate code point in
U+D800 through U+DFFF exists only to pair UTF-16 halves and is not a
Unicode scalar value.  A value above U+10FFFF is outside Unicode
altogether.

`synth_utf8_get` also derived `nbytes` from the leading byte without
bounding `nbytes` at four, so a 0xf8 or 0xfc leading byte produced a
five-byte or six-byte sequence.  UTF-8 encodes a Unicode scalar value
in at most four bytes, so no five-byte or six-byte sequence is valid.

Reject all four cases.  `synth_utf8_get` already returns -1 for an
invalid sequence and already reports a byte count in `*consumed`, so
both callers of `synth_utf8_get` need no change.

Signed-off-by: Brandon McGinty <brandon.mcginty@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c
index 3e42977..58f5ca5 100644
--- a/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c
+++ b/drivers/accessibility/speakup/synth.c
@@ -246,7 +246,15 @@ s32 synth_utf8_get(const char *buf, size_t count, size_t *consumed, size_t *want
 		return c;
 
 	default:
-		/* 2..6-byte UTF-8 */
+		/*
+		 * UTF-8 encodes a Unicode scalar value in at most four bytes,
+		 * so a five-byte or six-byte sequence cannot encode one.
+		 */
+		if (nbytes > 4) {
+			*consumed = 1;
+			*want = 1;
+			return -1;
+		}
 
 		if (count < nbytes) {
 			/* We don't have it all */
@@ -272,6 +280,20 @@ s32 synth_utf8_get(const char *buf, size_t count, size_t *consumed, size_t *want
 
 		*consumed = nbytes;
 		*want = 1;
+
+		/*
+		 * Reject an overlong form, because an overlong form encodes a
+		 * value that a shorter sequence already encodes.  Reject a
+		 * surrogate code point and a value above U+10FFFF, because
+		 * neither is a Unicode scalar value.
+		 */
+		if ((nbytes == 2 && value < 0x80) ||
+		    (nbytes == 3 && value < 0x800) ||
+		    (nbytes == 4 && value < 0x10000) ||
+		    (value >= 0xd800 && value <= 0xdfff) ||
+		    value > 0x10ffff)
+			return -1;
+
 		return value;
 	}
 }
